									</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4558017&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609055496" alt="Grigori Karpin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4558017)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/grigori-karpin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4558017); return false;" >Grigori Karpin</a></span> <span class="odate time_1609054305 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Dec 2020 07:31</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-89000/help:ideas-critique">Writing Help / Help: Ideas Critique</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13932651/llun-man-seeking-greenlight">LLUN Man Seeking Greenlight</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4854740">
									

<p>you're going about it wrong. If you want to keep the article mysterious, that makes sense. It does not make sense to keep the idea post mysterious.</p>
<p>The purpose of the greenlighting process is to convince at least two authors that you can communicate your idea in a compelling manner.</p>
<p>So&#8230; I am not concerned that you would not explain the aura in the idea post, I am concerned that it seems to have no connection to the anomalies as presented. I feel like you missed the point of my critique.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I think you need to sit down and simplify, make a cohesive anomaly about the one man and focus on his anomalous aspects that thematically connect to each other.</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>When I said this ^ it was not to suggest anything but that your idea felt too disjointed and you should simplify the core anomaly to make more cohesive sense.</em></p>
<p>You need to develop a cohesive proposal for the idea to communicate what your story is about.</p>
<p>No one is going to greenlight your concept without you explaining the concept. If you choose to withold and say something like &quot;you'll learn about it in the article&quot; I wouldn't trust that this will turn into an article that could survive.</p>

							</div>

								
					
