<p>Hey author, just pitching in my 2 cents.</p>
<p>This is really out of character for Anderson Robotics. Though this is not the first time they make an <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/new-buteo-series-mechanical-exoskeleton">exoskeleton</a>, it's certainly the first time they would be making a weapon of war! They're mostly known for making consumer grade products and fancy gizmos for the wealthy. A fighting exoskeleton that commits war crimes is definitely not something they would do. But that isn't to say Anderson Robotics isn't a moral bastion. Vincent Anderson, the founder, is known for being a cheat and a bit of a ruffian. There's also the fact that most AR products are powered by souls, which can lead to ethical questions.</p>
<p>Then there's the issue of the idea. Like zyn said, it's very typical of exoskeleton tropes and doesn't have much of interest going on for it.</p>

