														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4854665">
									

<p>Thank you for the critique. After several days of brainstorming I came up with the idea of a researcher obsessed with finding his own point of view. He'd try to use d-classes to flip the channels for him. Once that proves to be ineffective as they'd only be able to get a couple million in a year, he opts to find ways to dampen the signal, he'd find out that a lead-lined room works and it decreases the range considerably to around 40 kilometers. After that he discovers a d-class pov, he'd get the d-class to stare into the tv. The d-class does and enters into the trance. The researcher shuts off the tv and after five minutes the d-class comes to, but the d-class can't remember anything, much to the researcher's frustration. Several days later, the d-class kills himself.</p>
<p>This piques the researcher's interest even more. &quot;what did he see that compelled him to commit suicide?&quot; So, much to the dismay of the other researchers, he finds his own pov.</p>
<p>The ending is from another researcher who writes that the first researcher looked very unaware of his surroundings, suffered terrible disassociation and ultimately killed himself. Concludes that any researcher who wishes to test the SCP must do under supervision from another researcher.</p>

							</div>

								
					
